WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.210
It sailed through space at an unimaginable
speed.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:09.960
A grand mechanical construction unlike anything
we’d ever see on our planet.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.220
A terrifying weapon to end all weapons.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:20.859
Oppenheimer said of the atomic bomb, “Now,
I am become death, the destroyer of worlds,”

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:26.899
but comparatively, this device made the atom
bomb look like little more than a cherry bomb.

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:32.449
This deadly machine’s orders were simple:
Take a direct course to earth, activate, and

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:34.390
wipe out all life.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.809
Leave the planet barren, with not even the
smallest squirming microbes remaining.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:45.450
And this device, this Destroyer, was more
than capable of accomplishing this task.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.640
It’d been smooth sailing for millions of
miles.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.219
All diagnostics were looking positive.

00:00:51.219 --> 00:00:56.460
Within a mere decade or so, the human race
would be purged from the cosmos.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:01.489
Then, faster than the pre-programmed destroyer
could react, a huge, yellowish-green shape

00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:03.000
appeared in front of it.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.830
The Destroyer’s mysterious creators, in
their not-quite-infinte intelligence, had

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:13.150
planned for all the major celestial bodies
in Earth’s solar system, including Jupiter,

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:19.390
but for reasons unknown, they hadn’t calculated
the presence of Io, Jupiter’s third-largest

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:20.760
Galilean moon.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.850
The Destroyer struck it at incredible speed,
causing a mighty explosion and completely

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:28.600
altering its perfect trajectory.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.390
Alarms were sounding as the Destroyer hurtled
down onto the lower atmosphere of Jupiter.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:35.480
This alteration was unprecedented.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:37.080
Mayday, mayday.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:42.770
In some distant galaxy, screens were flashing
red, and the Creators suddenly registered

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.170
that this mission may not be so simple after
all.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:48.720
They would need to make adjustments.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.530
The impact into Jupiter triggered the Destroyer’s
attack protocol: Drawing from its limitless

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:59.420
energy source, it activated its hyper-advanced
anti-matter weaponry, causing spacial disruptions

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:04.780
and atmospheric shifts that created a huge,
red vortex on the surface of the gas giant,

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:09.710
one that would later become known to earth
based astronomers as the Great Red Spot.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:17.410
It’s 16,350 kilometers wide, which is 1.3
times the size of planet earth, and exists

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:21.450
as a kind of hell that almost no being could
endure.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:27.020
A constant, swirling nightmare with 432 km/h
wind speeds.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:32.160
In other words, the exact kind of nightmare
it would have turned earth into if ever it

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:35.610
had reached its actual intended destination.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.730
But no matter.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:41.890
This was just a minor setback, all things
considered - Such contingencies had been planned

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.390
for from the start.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.140
The Creators, back in the Triangulum Galaxy,
roughly three million light years away from

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:53.960
the Milky Way, simply began transmitting new
orders to the crashed, malfunctioning Destroyer:

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.960
“Unit is damaged: Repair.”

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.250
And that’s exactly what it began to do.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:04.730
It’s unknown how they were able to communicate,
let alone travel over such a vast distance,

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.860
but systems that would be impossible to even
explain to humans suddenly began to kick in.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:15.280
It released a legion of hardy, self-made octopoid
repair drones that began to search for the

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.400
machine’s missing parts, presumably hidden
within the gasses of Jupiter or pulled in

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.140
by the gravity of its nearby moons.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.520
Other drones would remain at the Destroyer’s
side, conducting repairs and guiding its vital

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.520
systems.

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:35.290
Presumably, to this machine and its creators,
humans are like mayflies: Insignificant creatures

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.350
with such tiny lifespans.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.320
Here today, gone tomorrow.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.600
The machine would conduct its repairs and
be upon us within a mere few centuries, barely

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.820
even diverting from the schedule.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:53.090
The one thing the creators didn’t anticipate
was the formation of a little organization

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:59.680
called the SCP Foundation, perhaps the only
hope humanity has in repelling this doomsday

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:00.680
weapon.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:05.130
The question we need to answer today is: Will
they be enough?

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:09.880
Terrifyingly, this device has been intent
on our destruction since long before the SCP

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.360
Foundation was even a glint in humanity’s
eye.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.629
It entered our solar system and crashed on
Jupiter all the way back in 1665.

00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:24.979
We know this thanks to the writings of Italian
Astronomer Giovanni Cassini, who recorded

00:04:24.979 --> 00:04:29.520
detailed notes in his journal on what we would
later dub SCP-2399.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:34.300
On October 8th, 1665, he wrote:

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.360
“I have observed something extraordinary
in the heavens.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:43.620
Last night, as I gazed through my looking
glass, I saw what appeared to be a star of

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:48.090
great luminescence streak through the far
reaches of our solar system.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:53.840
I have never recorded an object moving so
fast; it had surpassed the outer planets in

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.909
fewer than two hours!

00:04:55.909 --> 00:05:01.189
As I watched, by my own two eyes, I saw it
slow as it closed on Jupiter, make a sharp

00:05:01.189 --> 00:05:04.190
turn, and disappear into the planet itself.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.430
I saw many bursts of light afterwards, but
although I continued to peer at it until the

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:13.009
Sun broke, I saw no additional disturbances
in the night sky.

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:17.819
I must continue to document these changes,
and will alert my colleagues when the day

00:05:17.819 --> 00:05:19.229
is upon me.”

00:05:19.229 --> 00:05:20.259
On October 15th:

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:25.529
“I took Peter to my observation point last
night, but a week from the night I saw the

00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:27.930
fire rain upon Jupiter in the heavens.

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:33.389
He brought along his own looking glass, and
together we aimed our view upon the giant.

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:36.229
To our surprise, a magnificent change has
occurred!

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:41.349
Where once the distant world only showed bands
of color, there is now a great red spot where

00:05:41.349 --> 00:05:44.830
the star came to rest on the surface of Jupiter.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.949
Peter was incredulous, of course, that such
an amazing discovery could have taken place

00:05:48.949 --> 00:05:50.469
before our very eyes.

00:05:50.469 --> 00:05:53.180
I will continue to take note of this.”

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.389
On October 18th:

00:05:54.389 --> 00:06:00.219
“Tonight as I peered through my looking
glass, I swear on my life that I observed

00:06:00.219 --> 00:06:05.509
what looked to me like explosions and starbursts
emanating from our red spot.

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:11.409
I fear my mind is playing tricks on me, for
there has been no record of such violent outbursts

00:06:11.409 --> 00:06:14.699
by a heavenly body since the dawn of astronomy.

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:20.280
I will consult with Peter on the morrow, and
hopefully glean from him some advice on the

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.280
matter.”

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.280
On October 19th:

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:23.800
“Peter sees the same as I!

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.400
As I approached him with my concerns, he leveled
the same with me, and through our following

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:33.199
discussion we concluded that it must be a
powerful reaction to the falling star I saw

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:36.800
upon the first night, and not a product of
our own shortcomings.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:43.650
I am left wondering what cataclysmic event
must be taking place upon our heavenly neighbour.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.809
Our work to document this must go on.”

00:06:45.809 --> 00:06:52.580
And the work of documenting SCP-2399 has indeed
gone on, for centuries.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:57.330
Just as the machine itself has never once
ceased in its extensive repairs.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:04.210
It was first spotted by modern humanity, and
by extension, the SCP Foundation, in 1963.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.779
As soon as the technology existed to send
satellites up to Jupiter, the Foundation began

00:07:08.779 --> 00:07:15.129
studying this frightening new foe up close,
trying to get the true measure of its abilities.

00:07:15.129 --> 00:07:20.319
They discovered that the weapon has a mysterious
internal power supply that seems impossible

00:07:20.319 --> 00:07:26.659
to run down, as well as an advanced targeting
system, self-repair abilities, anti-matter

00:07:26.659 --> 00:07:29.879
weapons, and matter-disrupting capabilities.

00:07:29.879 --> 00:07:33.910
It also appears to have advanced shielding
systems that make destroying it currently

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:34.979
impossible.

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:40.930
And seeing as it’s a massive piece of military
machinery 514.18 million miles away from earth,

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.509
it’s impossible to truly contain.

00:07:43.509 --> 00:07:48.830
That’s why the Foundation has rearranged
its priorities into two new prongs regarding

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.830
SCP-2399.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.990
The first is suppressing information to avoid
panic.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:58.409
In order to achieve this, the Foundation has
embedded agents in all major observatories

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:03.490
to suppress any sightings of the machine,
and has also been conducting an active disinformation

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:06.569
campaign to keep it out of the public consciousness.

00:08:06.569 --> 00:08:11.139
The second prong of their containment procedure
is cutting off the transmissions between the

00:08:11.139 --> 00:08:15.759
Destroyer’s creators in the Triangulum Galaxy,
and the Destroyer itself.

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:21.120
Actually achieving this goal took a miraculous
feat in aerospace engineering: The BARRIER

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.149
Satellite Array.

00:08:22.149 --> 00:08:27.439
This was an unprecedented long-range satellite
array positioned in Jupiter’s higher orbit,

00:08:27.439 --> 00:08:32.320
designed for the specific purpose of blocking
the electromagnetic transmissions inbound

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.680
for the Destroyer.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:38.630
These messages are intercepted, decoded, and
logged on the Foundation database.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:43.659
The satellites have also been granted some
minor offensive capabilities for use in extreme

00:08:43.659 --> 00:08:45.180
emergencies.

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:50.199
SCP-2399 has been given the Keter Class due
to its unique containment difficulties.

00:08:50.199 --> 00:08:56.100
It’s also been given Disruption Class Amida,
for the hefty possibility that reaching earth

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.519
could result in an SK-Class “Barren Earth”
End of the World Scenario.

00:09:01.519 --> 00:09:06.079
On top of that, it has been given the risk
class “Danger”, due to the very high potential

00:09:06.079 --> 00:09:08.750
of all this actually coming to pass.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.720
The biggest concern for the Foundation at
present is the accelerating rate of repair

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:15.440
that the Destroyer seems to be exhibiting.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.389
Back when they first observed the Destroyer
up close, it was repairing itself at a rate

00:09:19.389 --> 00:09:20.540
of .12%.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:26.220
However, that rate of repair has now risen
to .78% annually.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:31.139
According to all known metrics, its current
level of functionality appears to be 59%.

00:09:31.139 --> 00:09:38.240
If ever it reaches 75%, then, to put it mildly,
we’re all going to be in a lot of trouble.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.931
Current projections say this is incredibly
likely to occur in the next 25 years, and

00:09:42.931 --> 00:09:47.810
if we don’t figure out a way to stop it
before then, the earth is doomed.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:52.720
The SCP Foundation received a chilling wake-up
call about the severity of the situation when

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.230
one of the BARRIER units noticed one of the
Destroyer’s repair drones zeroing in on

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:02.230
a piece of debris that seemed to be a part
of the Destroyer’s communications array.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:05.899
Considering that the Foundation’s main weapon
against the Destroyer right now is blocking

00:10:05.899 --> 00:10:10.540
its communication capabilities, allowing it
to repair its communications array would be

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.129
an unacceptable failure.

00:10:13.129 --> 00:10:18.329
Because of this, BARRIER Unit 53 was ordered
to fire its onboard concussion batteries at

00:10:18.329 --> 00:10:23.050
the drone in hopes of destroying it or at
least impeding its progress.

00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:27.779
This was met by swift and severe prevention
and retaliation from the Destroyer.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:33.060
It fired its own defensive charges, destroying
BARRIER Unit 53’s payload five kilometers

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:34.940
away from the repair drone.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:39.839
It subsequently destroyed BARRIER Unit 53,
as well as several other BARRIER satellites

00:10:39.839 --> 00:10:42.810
that just so happened to be in its vicinity.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:47.730
This led to an order that no BARRIER Units
are permitted to engage the repair drones,

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.709
for fear that this would lead to even greater
losses.

00:10:50.709 --> 00:10:56.889
The next attempt to fight back against SCP-2399
went by the name Project Gigas.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:11:02.170
This was a joint project between the SCP Foundation
and 45 different nations, with the goal of

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:09.440
using sheer, raw firepower to destroy or at
least utterly incapacitate SCP-2399.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:15.290
They would place almost 100 massive nuclear
warheads on Europa, Jupiter’s smallest Galilean

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:20.889
Moon, each one fitted with EMP detonators
to impede the Destroyer’s defense systems.

00:11:20.889 --> 00:11:26.040
They would hit it with so much nuclear hellfire
that surely it would be destroyed.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.569
Naturally, when this failed to meaningfully
damage the Destroyer, the Foundation returned

00:11:30.569 --> 00:11:35.170
to the drawing board, daunted by the enormity
of the task before them.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:40.829
The way they saw it, there was only one viable
option left: Protocol LEGIONNAIRE.

00:11:40.829 --> 00:11:45.339
Randall McAllan, the director of the BARRIER
Project, released the following haunting memo

00:11:45.339 --> 00:11:46.860
on the subject:

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:48.930
“So, SCP-2399.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:54.810
Have you ever sat and wondered, maybe after
you hear about a car accident on a street

00:11:54.810 --> 00:12:00.560
you were just on, or a bombing in a city you
were visiting, just how lucky you are to be

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.560
alive?

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:05.010
Just how many things have to go right for
you to continue to exist?

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:10.250
A few seconds too late, a few seconds too
early, and somebody reaches for something

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:16.279
they dropped and a busload of people run into
another busload of people.

00:12:16.279 --> 00:12:21.029
Sometimes this kind of thing does happen,
as we've seen, far too often.

00:12:21.029 --> 00:12:22.589
But that's what we're here for.

00:12:22.589 --> 00:12:26.600
To protect those who can't protect themselves
from things that they wouldn't even know to

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.350
protect themselves from.

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.810
We can't do it all, though.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.769
As many things as we've been able to contain,
as many things as we've been able to keep

00:12:33.769 --> 00:12:38.779
under lock that would threaten to destroy
us all, still far too many remain that we

00:12:38.779 --> 00:12:41.019
can't do anything about.

00:12:41.019 --> 00:12:47.129
Whether they're too big, or too fast, or too
powerful, any of these things could blink

00:12:47.129 --> 00:12:50.510
and wipe humanity from existence.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:54.480
The fact that they haven't done so yet is
just luck.

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:58.449
SCP-2399, however, is different.

00:12:58.449 --> 00:13:05.970
We have little information regarding SCP-2399's
motives, origins, and full capabilities.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:11.150
We do not understand how it is capable of
communicating over such large distances, or

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:17.930
why those who constructed it (if it was, in
fact, constructed) sent it to us in the first

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:18.930
place.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:24.720
We do not know what would happen if SCP-2399
is able to fully repair itself, or if part

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:28.050
of our array would break down and a message
would get through.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:32.230
We do not know this, so we must assume the
worst.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:37.670
Judging by what we've seen, were SCP-2399
to have reached Earth, it would have led to

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.110
our timely destruction.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:43.730
But sometimes humanity gets a little help.

00:13:43.730 --> 00:13:46.560
Sometimes something steps in the way of the
apocalypse.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.139
For us, and for SCP-2399, it was Jupiter.

00:13:51.139 --> 00:13:56.649
As SCP-2399 began to slow on its approach
to Earth, Cassini saw what we've been able

00:13:56.649 --> 00:14:04.339
to ascertain; that SCP-2399 struck Io, was
damaged, and was unable to escape the gravitational

00:14:04.339 --> 00:14:05.920
pull of Jupiter.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:11.610
Its weapons activated as they were intended,
but it was Jupiter that experienced doomsday,

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:12.970
not us.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:19.760
Eventually, though, it's likely that SCP-2399
will resume full functionality, and will likely

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:23.589
be able to pull away from Jupiter and proceed
to its target.

00:14:23.589 --> 00:14:29.910
As of now, we can keep hurling bombs and EMPs
at it all we want, but we've got no indication

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:35.379
that any of it will so much as scratch the
thing, on the contrary, experience dictates

00:14:35.379 --> 00:14:36.990
it would do nothing at all.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:41.819
If this were to happen now, we would undoubtedly
be destroyed.

00:14:41.819 --> 00:14:44.449
Jupiter has given us time.

00:14:44.449 --> 00:14:52.230
For now, SCP-2399 will remain there, reassembling
itself, while we devise some way to stop it.

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:55.930
Like it or not, we are in an arms race with
this thing.

00:14:55.930 --> 00:15:00.900
Our best guesses give us something like 25
years until it is able to hear past our dampening

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:01.900
array.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.759
Until then, we must seize the opportunity
that has been laid before us.

00:15:05.759 --> 00:15:10.660
We must use the time we have been given, and
not let it be wasted.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.290
So we devised Protocol LEGIONNAIRE.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:18.720
One gigantic EMP, powered by god-knows-what,
followed by a volley of nukes big enough to

00:15:18.720 --> 00:15:21.790
wipe out our civilization a thousand times
over.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:25.590
A blunt plan, and simple, and likely futile.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.199
Our researchers, and researchers around the
globe, have yet to devise even a way to deliver

00:15:30.199 --> 00:15:33.769
that kind of pulse, let alone a way to power
it.

00:15:33.769 --> 00:15:38.470
There is no indication whatsoever that we
will be able to complete LEGIONNAIRE on time,

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:42.490
or if it will do what is intended once it
is completed.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:43.980
But we must try.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:46.019
We must do something.

00:15:46.019 --> 00:15:50.470
Even if we have to drain our banks and empty
our mines, we must try.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:55.769
Not often do we get a chance to see the swerving
bus that will end our lives, and step out

00:15:55.769 --> 00:15:56.769
of the way.

00:15:56.769 --> 00:16:00.220
Jupiter, unknowingly, has offered us that
chance.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:02.410
I suggest we take it.”

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:07.120
You’re probably wondering: Why is McAllan
approaching this situation with such desperate

00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:08.120
urgency?

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:14.129
Well, it’s because in 1996, and again in
2015, the message that the Destroyer has been

00:16:14.129 --> 00:16:16.420
receiving changed.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:19.270
It was no longer a simple order to repair.

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:27.910
The message now read “Unit is out of range
of target: Proceed to planet #3 in system.

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:30.850
Priority is target: Cease repairs.”

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:36.360
And if that message ever gets through, time
is already up for all of us.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:42.269
Now go check out “SCP-001 Ouroboros Cycle
- The Full Story Compilation” and “SCP

00:16:42.269 --> 00:16:46.820
XK Class End of the World Scenarios Explained”
for more anomalies that could wipe us off

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.149
the face of the earth!

